  "id": "concussion",
  "term": "concussion",
  "definition": "Concussion is a mild traumatic brain injury, often discussed in sports, that briefly disrupts normal brain function but can also leave subtle effects that last for months or years after obvious symptoms have gone away. Repeated concussions are linked with cumulative problems in brain and cognitive functions, including attention, motor learning, mood, sleep, and sensorimotor performance.",
